 "about": "End of the page, the menu opened and closed in one take (cap-end-openclose, 2026-10-10; article clip). Built from fixes/g0-box/phone/g-fastshort-g0.json: reload, 4 s, mark approach, 12 fixed drags up (520 px in 1200 ms, 300 ms apart: the passes the original always ran and g0 builds need 11 of), a y>=3000 guard before each down stroke (the compiler's pull-to-refresh rule; met within ~10 ms on both builds, fails only a run whose page left the end), 1.5 s, mark reset, the slow close drag that precedes E21 in fastshort (450 px down in 2000 ms, held 300 ms), 2.5 s at rest; then two cycles of: open push as E21 (up 60 px in 50 ms, fling), a FIXED 2.0 s, close push as E22 (down 120 px in 60 ms, fling), a fixed 2.0 s (1.0 s after the last, mark after-1s), and 1 s more at rest (mark done). No atEnd or settled waits inside the window, so the pushes come on the same clock on both builds (the runner's own still-page check before a down stroke or an up stroke at the end, ~0.1 s, stays). Same input on both arms; fixed before any capture.",
